---
import OdeV2Layout from '../../../layouts/OdeV2Layout.astro';
import DataTag from '../../../components/ode-v2/DataTag.astro';
import Status from '../../../components/ode-v2/Status.astro';
import Doors from '../../../components/ode-v2/Doors.astro';
import Finding from '../../../components/ode-v2/Finding.astro';
import { odeMeta, odeRoutes } from '../../../i18n/ode-v2';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const m = odeMeta[lang].home;
const r = odeRoutes[lang];

const doors = [
  {
    who: 'Investor',
    question: 'Is there a defensible position, and which risks are already stated?',
    href: r.investitori,
    cta: 'The verdict, in two parts',
    next: 'Then: Position, where OdE can and cannot exist.',
  },
  {
    who: 'Research partner',
    question: 'Are the questions real, does the method hold, and is there something to publish?',
    href: r.evidenza,
    cta: 'The open questions',
    next: 'Then: the Audit, that is, what we have already verified.',
  },
  {
    who: 'Commercial partner',
    question: 'What am I actually buying, and what can I claim without exposing myself?',
    href: r.tesi,
    cta: 'The parameter that decides',
    next: 'Then: AMSA and Regulation.',
  },
];

const limits = [
  {
    kind: 'contro' as const,
    t: 'There is no clinical evidence on topical tallow',
    d: 'No high-grade study of the cutaneous effect of tallow applied as such. This is not a shortcoming of our search: it is the state of the field, and it applies to us too.',
  },
  {
    kind: 'contro' as const,
    t: 'Our material changes on the skin, and we do not know in which direction',
    d: 'Skin bacteria secrete lipases that cleave triglycerides. Petrolatum, mineral oil, squalane and dimethicone have none: they are inert, we are not. What is released is a mixture, and for its two main components the evidence points in opposite directions. The net effect has never been measured.',
  },
  {
    kind: 'contro' as const,
    t: 'The market where the difference matters is small, and we cannot size it',
    d: 'Where tallow is bought in volume we cannot compete on price. Where qualification matters, volumes are small and no public data separates them.',
  },
];
---
<OdeV2Layout title={m.title} description={m.description} lang={lang}>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="ode-eyebrow hero-eyebrow">
      Systematic search across twelve bibliographic basins, in six languages
    </p>
    <h1>
      There is no clinical study measuring what tallow does to human skin.
    </h1>
    <p class="hero-lede">
      None. Not a weak one, not an old one, not one in a language nobody reads. We searched
      twelve databases in six languages before accepting it, and before building a company on
      top of it.
      <DataTag kind="fonte" label="Gap verified by searching twelve basins: PubMed, EMBASE, Europe PMC, Scopus, Web of Science, Google Scholar, Semantic Scholar, ClinicalTrials.gov, CIR, CosIng, EUR-Lex and the FAO Codex Alimentarius. Targeted searches in Polish, Russian, Chinese, Japanese and Turkish in addition to English. Research track 5 v3.0, sections 1.3 and 8." />
    </p>
    <p class="hero-status"><Status kind="lacuna" lang={lang} /></p>

    <div class="thesis">
      <p class="thesis-line">
        If nothing is known and nobody is measuring, the value is not in the tallow.
        <strong>It is in being able to qualify it.</strong>
      </p>
      <p class="thesis-sub">
        OdE does not sell tallow. It sells certainty about what is inside a batch of tallow.
        In a market where nobody measures, whoever measures first defines the standard.
        We are a laboratory before we are a producer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-label="Three doors">
    <p class="ode-eyebrow block-eyebrow">Three audiences, three different questions</p>
    <Doors doors={doors} />
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-label="The verification work">
    <p class="ode-eyebrow block-eyebrow">What we verified</p>
    <div class="verif">
      <div class="verif-text">
        <p>
          Before describing a product we spent months trying to break the idea. The result is an
          evidence library with graded records, persistent identifiers, and gaps documented with
          the query and the basin that produced them. It includes an audit of the most cited
          review in the field, which anyone can repeat in an afternoon.
        </p>
        <p class="note">
          It is the work no competitor can copy without redoing it, and the only reason we
          believe we are entitled to talk about this material at all.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="verif-cta" href={r.audit}>
        <span class="verif-cta-k">The Audit</span>
        <span class="verif-cta-d">The evidence gap, the matrix error in the most cited review, the taxonomy of claims that do not hold.</span>
        <span class="verif-cta-a" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-label="Stated limits">
    <p class="ode-eyebrow block-eyebrow">Three limits, before you find them yourself</p>
    <p class="measure block-intro">
      A stated risk raises the credibility of everything else. A limit discovered alone destroys
      it. These three are the most serious, and they are on the home page on purpose.
    </p>
    <ul class="limits">
      {limits.map((l) => (
        <li>
          <Finding kind={l.kind} lang={lang} />
          <h2>{l.t}</h2>
          <p>{l.d}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      The full picture, unsoftened, is in <a href={r.posizione}>Position</a> and
      <a href={r.investitori}>Investors</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block block--last" aria-label="What OdE is">
    <p class="ode-eyebrow block-eyebrow">In one line</p>
    <p class="closing">
      A laboratory that qualifies and certifies an ingredient batch by batch, in a category that
      has no standard yet. The tallow is the carrier. The document is the product.
    </p>
  </section>
</OdeV2Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 1rem 0 2.4rem; max-width: 48rem; }
  .hero-eyebrow { margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5.2vw, 3.3rem); letter-spacing: -0.015em; line-height: 1.08; }
  .hero-lede { font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.62; color: var(--ode-body); margin: 1.3rem 0 0; max-width: 40rem; }
  .hero-status { margin: 1rem 0 0; }

  .thesis {
    margin: 2.2rem 0 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.7rem;
    background: var(--green-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--green-border);
    border-radius: var(--ode-radius);
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
  .thesis-line { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.4vw, 1.45rem); line-height: 1.35; color: var(--ink); margin: 0; font-weight: 300; }
  .thesis-line strong { font-weight: 500; }
  .thesis-sub { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body); margin: 0.9rem 0 0; }

  .block { padding: 2.3rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--ode-rule); }
  .block--last { padding-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .block-eyebrow { margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }
  .block-intro { margin: 0 0 1.4rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body); }

  .verif { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr; gap: 1.8rem; align-items: start; }
  .verif-text p { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.62; color: var(--body); max-width: 34rem; }
  .verif-text .note { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .verif-cta {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    grid-template-areas: 'k a' 'd d';
    gap: 0.5rem 0.8rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--ode-radius);
    padding: 1.3rem 1.4rem;
    transition: border-color 160ms ease, transform 160ms ease;
  }
  .verif-cta:hover { border-color: var(--accent); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .verif-cta-k { grid-area: k; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); }
  .verif-cta-a { grid-area: a; color: var(--accent); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .verif-cta-d { grid-area: d; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--body); }

  .limits { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.4rem 1.8rem; }
  .limits h2 { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); margin: 0.6rem 0 0.45rem; line-height: 1.35; }
  .limits p { font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--body); margin: 0; }

  .closing { font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.2vw, 1.3rem); line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 300; color: var(--ink); max-width: 40rem; margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 780px) { .verif { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.3rem; } }
</style>
